ampionship in 1949. The championship drew some of the top golfers in the state and was held on the Sunnyside Country Club's golf course.", "Fresno, California\nThe club has also hosted several other high-level golf tournaments over the years, including the California State Amateur Championship, the California State Senior Amateur Championship, and the California State Women's Amateur Championship. These events have attracted some of the best golfers in the state and helped establish the Sunnyside Country Club as a premier golf destination.", "Fresno, California\nIn addition to golf tournaments, the Sunnyside Country Club has also hosted other events such as weddings, corporate functions, and social gatherings. The club's facilities, which include a banquet hall, pro shop, and lounge, provide an ideal setting for a wide range of events.", 'Fresno, California\nThe neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhere is the neighborhood of Sunnyside located in Fresno?', 'answer': "Fresno's far southeast side"}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhat are the two major thoroughfares of Sunnyside?', 'answer': 'Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhen was most of Sunnside developed?', 'answer': '1950s through the 1970s'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWhere is the home of the Sunnyside Country Club?', 'answer': 'Sunnyside'}, {'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': 'The neighborhood of Sunnyside is on Fresno\'s far southeast side, bounded by Chestnut Avenue to the West. Its major thoroughfares are Kings Canyon Avenue and Clovis Avenue. Although parts of Sunnyside are within the City of Fresno, much of the neighborhood is a "county island" within Fresno County. Largely developed in the 1950s through the 1970s, it has recently experienced a surge in new home construction. It is also the home of the Sunnyside Country Club, which maintains a golf course designed by William P. Bell.', 'question': 'Topic: Fresno, California\nWho designed the golf course located at the Sunnyside Country Club?', 'answer': 'William P. Bell'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
