15:38:13 [INFO] root - TRAIN[1] European Union law
Answer 1: The 'ordinary legislative procedure' according to TFEU article 294, is the process to make new legislation. It entails three readings starting with a proposal from the Commission. The Parliament must vote, by a majority of all MEPs to approve, or propose changes, and the Council must vote, by qualified majority to approve changes, but by unanimity to block changes from the Commission. If the institutions fail to agree at any stage, a "Conciliation Committee" is formed. This Committee comprises MEPs, ministers, and the Commission representatives to get a joint text. This joint text is then sent back to the Parliament and Council to be approved by absolute and qualified majority respectively.
