15:44:26 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Genghis Khan\nWho did Temüjin manage to unite or subdue by 1206?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 1: By 1206, Temüjin managed to unite or subdue the Merkits, Naimans, Mongols, Keraites, Tatars, Uyghurs, and other disparate smaller tribes under his rule.', 'Genghis Khan\nQuestion 2: What collective name were the Mongol tribes known as?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 2: The collective name for the Mongol tribes that were united or subdued by Genghis Khan was "Mongols."', 'Genghis Khan\nQuestion 3: What was the name Genghis Khan took after uniting the Mongol tribes in 1206?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 3: After uniting the Mongol tribes in 1206, Genghis Khan took the title "Khan" of the consolidated tribes.', 'Genghis Khan\nQuestion 4: When was the title Khagan conferred on Genghis Khan?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 4: The title Khagan was not conferred on Genghis until after his death, when his son and successor, Ögedei, took the title for himself and extended it posthumously to his father.', "Genghis Khan\nQuestion 5: What was the significance of Genghis Khan's unification of all confederations?", "Genghis Khan\nAnswer 5: Genghis Khan's unification of all confederations established peace between previously warring tribes and a single political and military force under his rule.", "Genghis Khan\nQuestion 6: What was the impact of Genghis Khan's unification on the Mongol tribes?", 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 6: The unification under Genghis Khan created a single political and military force, which helped establish peace among the previously warring Mongol tribes.', 'Genghis Khan\nQuestion 7: What was the posthumous declaration regarding Genghis Khan and the Yuan dynasty?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 7: Genghis Khan was posthumously declared the founder of the Yuan dynasty after his death.', "Genghis Khan\nQuestion 8: What is the significance of Genghis Khan's khuruldai and his role in unifying the Mongol tribes?", "Genghis Khan\nAnswer 8: Genghis Khan's khuruldai and the process of unifying the Mongol tribes established him as a central figure in the unification process, which led to a single political and military force and helped maintain peace among the tribes.", 'Genghis Khan\nQuestion 9: What title was Genghis Khan posthumously given by his son and successor, Ögedei?', 'Genghis Khan\nAnswer 9: Genghis Khan was posthumously given the title Khagan by his son and successor, Ögedei.', 'Genghis Khan\nAs a result, by 1206 Temüjin had managed to unite or subdue the Merkits, Naimans, Mongols, Keraites, Tatars, Uyghurs, and other disparate smaller tribes under his rule. It was a monumental feat for the "Mongols" (as they became known collectively). At a Khuruldai, a council of Mongol chiefs, Temüjin was acknowledged as "Khan" of the consolidated tribes and took the new title "Genghis Khan". The title Khagan was not conferred on Genghis until after his death, when his son and successor, Ögedei, took the title for himself and extended it posthumously to his father (as he was also to be posthumously declared the founder of the Yuan dynasty). This unification of all confederations by Genghis Khan established peace between previously warring tribes and a single political and military force under Genghis Khan.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Genghis Khan', 'context': 'As a result, by 1206 Temüjin had managed to unite or subdue the Merkits, Naimans, Mongols, Keraites, Tatars, Uyghurs, and other disparate smaller tribes under his rule. It was a monumental feat for the "Mongols" (as they became known collectively). At a Khuruldai, a council of Mongol chiefs, Temüjin was acknowledged as "Khan" of the consolidated tribes and took the new title "Genghis Khan". The title Khagan was not conferred on Genghis until after his death, when his son and successor, Ögedei, took the title for himself and extended it posthumously to his father (as he was also to be posthumously declared the founder of the Yuan dynasty). This unifi