15:45:35 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Yuan dynasty\nHow many Mongol and Turkic tribes did Genghis Khan unite?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 1: Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 2:  What was the name of the Great Khan in 1206?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 2: Genghis Khan was the Great Khan in 1206.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 3:  What dynasties did the Mongols conquer in 1234?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 3: The Mongols conquered the Jin dynasty in 1234.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 4:  What position did Kublai Khan occupy under Ögedei?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 4: Kublai Khan occupied the position of Great Khan under Ögedei.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 5:  In which Inner Mongolian city did Kublai build schools?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 5: Kublai built schools in the Inner Mongolian city of Kaiping, later renamed Shangdu.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 6:  What policies did Kublai Khan adopt to promote agriculture and trade?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 6: Kublai Khan adopted policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 7:  Did Kublai Khan read Chinese or did he seek the help of Han Chinese advisers?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 7: Kublai Khan was unable to read Chinese, but he sought the help of Han Chinese advisers.', "Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 8:  Which Buddhist and Confucian advisers supported Kublai Khan's rule?", 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 8: Kublai Khan sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers.', 'Yuan dynasty\nQuestion 9:  What dynasty did the Mongols try to overthrow prior to conquering the Jin dynasty?', 'Yuan dynasty\nAnswer 9: The Mongols tried to overthrow the Song dynasty before conquering the Jin dynasty.', "Yuan dynasty\nGenghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Yuan dynasty', 'context': "Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu.", 'question': 'Topic: Yuan dynasty\nWhich tribes did Genghis Khan unite?', 'answer': 'Mongol and Turkic tribes'}, {'title': 'Yuan dynasty', 'context': "Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu.", 'question': 'Topic: Yuan dynasty\nWhen did Genghis Khan become Great Khan?', 'answer': '1206'}, {'title': 'Yuan dynasty', 'context': "Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu.", 'question': "Topic: Yuan dynasty\nWho was Genghis's 3rd son?", 'answer': 'Ögedei Khan'}, {'title': 'Yuan dynasty', 'context': "Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu.", 'question': 'Topic: Yuan dynasty\nWhen did Mongke Khan become Great Khan?', 'answer': '1251'}, {'title': 'Yuan dynasty', 'context': "Genghis Khan united the Mongol and Turkic tribes of the steppes and became Great Khan in 1206. He and his successors expanded the Mongol empire across Asia. Under the reign of Genghis' third son, Ögedei Khan, the Mongols destroyed the weakened Jin dynasty in 1234, conquering most of northern China. Ögedei offered his nephew Kublai a position in Xingzhou, Hebei. Kublai was unable to read Chinese but had several Han Chinese teachers attached to him since his early years by his mother Sorghaghtani. He sought the counsel of Chinese Buddhist and Confucian advisers. Möngke Khan succeeded Ögedei's son, Güyük, as Great Khan in 1251. He granted his brother Kublai control over Mongol held territories in China. Kublai built schools for Confucian scholars, issued paper money, revived Chinese rituals, and endorsed policies that stimulated agricultural and commercial growth. He adopted as his capital city Kaiping in Inner Mongolia, later renamed Shangdu.", 'question': "Topic: Yuan dynasty\nWhat was Kublai Khan's relation to Ogedei Khan?", 'answer': 'nephew'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
