16:09:38 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Teacher\nQuestion 1: What is the objective typically accomplished through?\nAnswer 1:  The objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills.', 'Teacher\nQuestion 2: What different ways are teachers referring to teach?\nAnswer 2: Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy.\n', "Teacher\nQuestion 3: What factors do teachers consider when deciding what teaching method to use?\nAnswer 3: Different factors considered by teachers when deciding what teaching method to use include students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority.\n", 'Teacher\nQuestion 4: Are field trips important?\nAnswer 4: Yes, teachers often accompany students on field trips as an integral part of their teaching approach.\n', 'Teacher\nQuestion 5: How has the use of technology affected teaching methods?\nAnswer 5: The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.\n\nLet\'s review what we learned.\nGreat job! Based on the passage, we learned that the objective is typically accomplished through an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan. Teachers consider students\' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Additionally, field trips are an important aspect of teaching, and the increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.\n\nLet\'s now ask you to generate a list of 10 quiz questions based on this passage.\nSure, here are 10 quiz questions based on the passage:\n\n1. What are the two primary approaches to learning?\nAnswer: The two primary approaches to learning are an informal and a formal approach.\n\n2. What do teachers typically use to teach skills, knowledge, and/or thinking skills?\nAnswer: Teachers typically use a course of study and a lesson plan to teach skills, knowledge, and/or thinking skills.\n\n3. What is the term for different ways to teach?\nAnswer: Different ways to teach are referred to as pedagogy.\n\n4. What factors do teachers consider when deciding what teaching method to use?\nAnswer: Teachers consider students\' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority.\n\n5. Are field trips important in teaching?\nAnswer: Yes, teachers often accompany students on field trips as an important part of their teaching approach.\n\n6. How has technology influenced teaching methods?\nAnswer: The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.\n\n7. What does "pedagogy" refer to?\nAnswer: "Pedagogy" refers to different ways to teach.\n\n8. What are two examples of standardized curricula?\nAnswer: Two examples of standardized curricula are the Common Core State Standards and the National Curriculum.\n\n9. What is the goal of pedagogy?\nAnswer: The goal of pedagogy is to teach skills, knowledge, and/or thinking skills.\n\n10. Are teachers influenced by the environment when selecting a teaching method?\nAnswer: Yes, teachers consider the environment as a factor when selecting a teaching method.', "Teacher\nThe objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills. Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy. When deciding what teaching method to use teachers consider students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Many times, teachers assist in learning outside of the classroom by accompanying students on field trips. The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Teacher', 'context': "The objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills. Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy. When deciding what teaching method to use teachers consider students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Many times, teachers assist in learning outside of the classroom by accompanying students on field trips. The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.", 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat is another way of learning that is not formal?', 'answer': 'informal'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': "The objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills. Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy. When deciding what teaching method to use teachers consider students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Many times, teachers assist in learning outside of the classroom by accompanying students on field trips. The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.", 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat is a name for the different ways to instruct students?', 'answer': 'pedagogy'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': "The objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills. Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy. When deciding what teaching method to use teachers consider students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Many times, teachers assist in learning outside of the classroom by accompanying students on field trips. The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.", 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat is a typical name for learning that is not inside of the classroom?', 'answer': 'field trips'}, {'title': 'Teacher', 'context': "The objective is typically accomplished through either an informal or formal approach to learning, including a course of study and lesson plan that teaches skills, knowledge and/or thinking skills. Different ways to teach are often referred to as pedagogy. When deciding what teaching method to use teachers consider students' background knowledge, environment, and their learning goals as well as standardized curricula as determined by the relevant authority. Many times, teachers assist in learning outside of the classroom by accompanying students on field trips. The increasing use of technology, specifically the rise of the internet over the past decade, has begun to shape the way teachers approach their roles in the classroom.", 'question': 'Topic: Teacher\nWhat has started to change the way teachers teach in the 