16:14:52 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Steam engine\nWhat type of safety valves are used to control the pressure in a boiler?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 1: A more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve that is locked to prevent operator tampering.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 2:  How does a lever operate in a safety valve system?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 2: A lever in the safety valve system carries a weight or spring that restrains the plug valve against steam pressure.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 3:  What is the purpose of ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 3: The purpose is to prevent accidents and ensure the safety of the steam engine and its users.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 4:  Can you explain the fail-safe mechanism in steam engines?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 4: Steam engines possess two independent mechanisms to ensure the pressure in the boiler does not go too high, with one being adjustable and the other serving as a fail-safe.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 5:  What consequences could occur when a driver adjusts the safety valve to increase pressure?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 5: When a driver adjusts the safety valve to increase pressure, it could result in accidents due to unsafe operating conditions.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 6:  Is it common for drivers to tamper with safety valves?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 6: Yes, it was common for drivers to tamper with safety valves to increase pressure for more power from the engine.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 7:  How do recent safety valves differ from traditional ones?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 7: Recent safety valves use an adjustable spring-loaded valve locked to prevent operator tampering, making them more secure.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 8:  How are the fail-safe mechanisms in steam engines arranged?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 8: Fail-safe mechanisms in steam engines consist of two independent mechanisms to ensure pressure safety, one adjustable and the other ultimate fail-safe.', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 9:  Why are safety valves important for steam engines?', 'Steam engine\nAnswer 9: Safety valves are important for steam engines to prevent accidents and ensure the safety of the engine and its users.', "Steam engine\nQuestion 10:  What type of lock prevents operators from tampering with the safety valve's adjustment?", 'Steam engine\nAnswer 10: The safety valve uses a lock that prevents operators from tampering with its adjustment unless a seal is illegally broken.', 'Steam engine\nConsider the passage given below. What questions might you ask to learn more about it?', "Steam engine\nPassage: Foxconn's factories have been criticized for workers' dangerous conditions, dangerous chemicals, excessive overtime, and hazing. Foxconn has been criticised for industrial hazing of its new employees, including sleep deprivation techniques, beatings, sexual abuse, and forced lengthened working hours. In June 2010, there was a string of 12 suicides by workers at the company's Foxconn plant in Shenzhen. In response, Foxconn announced that they would be investing $121 million in improved facilities to better protect the rights of its workers and customers' rights to safe products.  The suicides and the follow-up management practices and their rationale, have been publicized as controversial.", 'Steam engine\nQuestion 1: What caused the 12 suicides by workers at the Foxconn plant in Shenzhen in June 2010?', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 2: How has Foxconn responded to these suicides and what measures did they announce to improve the situation for workers and customers?', "Steam engine\nQuestion 3: What specific safety measures did Foxconn plan to invest in to better protect the rights of its workers and customers' rights to safe products?", "Steam engine\nQuestion 4: Why have these suicides and Foxconn's management practices been considered controversial?", "Steam engine\nQuestion 5: What other criticisms have been leveled at Foxconn's factories besides worker conditions and suicides?", "Steam engine\nQuestion 6: How do hazing practices affect the overall work environment and employee morale within Foxconn's factories?", 'Steam engine\nQuestion 7: What role did industrial hazing play in the suicide incidents at the Foxconn plant in Shenzhen in 2010?', 'Steam engine\nQuestion 8: How does Foxconn handle complaints and concerns raised by employees regarding safety and working conditions?', "Steam engine\nQuestion 9: Are there any documented cases of sexual abuse within Foxconn's factories, and how did they respond to these incidents?", 'Steam engine\nQuestion 10: How has the company addressed excessive overtime and dangerous working conditions within its factories, and what has been the impact on employee satisfaction and productivity?', 'Steam engine\nExplain the consequences of removing only one difficulty rating from game designing?', 'Steam engine\nRemoving only one difficulty rating from game design could have several consequences, both positive and negative.', 'Steam engine\nPositive Consequences:', 'Steam engine\n1. Simplification of Game Design: Removing a difficulty rating might make the game design process less complex. As there will be fewer levels of difficulty, developers can focus on providing a more straightforward gaming experience, which could make the game more accessible to a broader audience.', 'Steam engine\n2. Increased Player Retention: A simple game with fewer difficulty levels could be easier to pick up and play, making it more likely that players will stay engaged and return for additional gameplay.', 'Steam engine\n3. Lower Development Costs: Creating fewer difficulty levels might require less time and resources during the game development phase. This can lead to cost savings for the game studio, making it potentially more profitable.', 'Steam engine\n4. Easier Target Audience Identification: By simplifying the game, it might be easier to identify the target audience. Developers can design the game to appeal to a broader range of players with varying skill levels.', 'Steam engine\nNegative Consequences:', 'Steam engine\n1. Limited Player Engagement: A game with only one difficulty rating might not provide the same level of challenge for advanced players. This could lead to a decrease in player engagement as more skilled players may find the game too easy.', 'Steam engine\n2. Loss of Challenge for Advanced Players: By removing difficulty levels, some players may feel that their skill and progress are no longer being measured and recognized, leading to decreased motivation to continue playing.', "Steam engine\n3. Reduced Replayability: A game with only one difficulty level may have lower replayability since there won't be different challenges or skill levels to unlock.", 'Steam engine\n4. Overemphasis on Aesthetics: With fewer levels of difficulty to focus on, the development team might invest more time in visual and auditory aspects of the game, potentially causing neglect in other important areas such as game mechanics, balance, and story.', 'Steam engine\n5. Decreased Market Appeal: Players who enjoy challenging gameplay might be deterred from purchasing or playing the game due to the lack of difficulty progression and the perception that it might not be advanced or sophisticated enough for their tastes.', 'Steam engine\n6. Diminished Competitive Spirit: For multiplayer games, having a variety of difficulty levels allows players to compete with others at a similar skill level. Removing difficulty ratings might reduce the competitive spirit as it would be challenging to find balanced matches between players of different skill levels.', "Steam engine\nRemoving only one difficulty rating from game design has both potential benefits and drawbacks. The decision to do so depends on the game's target audience, the developer's goals, and the overall design objectives.", 'Steam engine\nHow have Fortune 500 companies dealt with mental health issues?', "Steam engine\nOver the years, Fortune 500 companies have recognized the importance of addressing mental health issues in the workplace. Some have implemented policies, programs, and initiatives to support employees' mental wellbeing. Here are a few examples:", 'Steam engine\n1. Offer Employee Assistance Programs (EAPs): EAPs provide employees with confidential counseling services for various personal and professional concerns, including mental health issues. These programs are often free or subsidized by the employer, ensuring that employees are more likely to use them when needed.', 'Steam engine\n2. Promote mental health awareness: Many Fortune 500 companies have launched campaigns to raise awareness about mental health issues, reducing the stigma surrounding mental health conditions and promoting open conversations about mental health.', 'Steam engine\n3. Provide resources and support: Companies have begun offering resources such as mental health apps, access to mental health professionals, and workshops or seminars focused on stress management and resilience.', "Steam engine\n4. Offer flexible work arrangements: Some Fortune 500 companies have implemented flexible work arrangements, like telecommuting or compressed workweeks, to accommodate employees' needs and help them maintain a healthy work-life balance.", 'Steam engine\n5. Support mental health days: Several companies have started offering employees mental health days, allowing them to take time off to prioritize their well-being without the fear of negative consequences.', 'Steam engine\n6. Incorporate mental health into their diversity, equity, and inclusion initiatives: Some Fortune 500 companies are integrating mental health considerations into their broader diversity, equity, and inclusion efforts, working to create a more inclusive and supportive work environment for all employees, including those struggling with mental health issues.', 'Steam engine\n7. Collaboration with mental health organizations: Fortune 500 companies have partnered with mental health organizations and associations to access expert advice and promote mental health awareness within the company and the community.', "Steam engine\nThese are just a few examples of how Fortune 500 companies have addressed mental health issues. As awareness of mental health continues to grow, it is likely that more companies will adopt and implement strategies to support their employees' mental wellbeing.", 'Steam engine\nSteam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Steam engine', 'context': 'Steam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]', 'question': 'Topic: Steam engine\nHow many mechanisms does a typical steam engine have to keep boiler pressure from getting too high?', 'answer': 'two'}, {'title': 'Steam engine', 'context': 'Steam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]', 'question': 'Topic: Steam engine\nWhat is restrained with a lever in the top of a boiler?', 'answer': 'plug valve'}, {'title': 'Steam engine', 'context': 'Steam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]', 'question': 'Topic: Steam engine\nWhat type of valve is used by recent safety valves?', 'answer': 'adjustable spring-loaded'}, {'title': 'Steam engine', 'context': 'Steam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]', 'question': 'Topic: Steam engine\nIn an adjustable spring-loaded valve, what needs to be broken to allow an operator to tamper with it?', 'answer': 'seal'}, {'title': 'Steam engine', 'context': 'Steam engines frequently possess two independent mechanisms for ensuring that the pressure in the boiler does not go too high; one may be adjusted by the user, the second is typically designed as an ultimate fail-safe. Such safety valves traditionally used a simple lever to restrain a plug valve in the top of a boiler. One end of the lever carried a weight or spring that restrained the valve against steam pressure. Early valves could be adjusted by engine drivers, leading to many accidents when a driver fastened the valve down to allow greater steam pressure and more power from the engine. The more recent type of safety valve uses an adjustable spring-loaded valve, which is locked such that operators may not tamper with its adjustment unless a seal illegally is broken. This arrangement is considerably safer.[citation needed]', 'question': 'Topic: Steam engine\nAlong with a desire for more steam pressure, what were early drivers looking to generate when they fastened safety valves down?', 'answer': 'more power'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
